        <body>
            <div xml:id="d575">

                <pb facs="0993" n="893" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg893"/>

                <head>No. 575.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-12-10"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 10,
                        1879</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 185.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 216, regarding the proposed law for the abolition of slavery in Cuba; and,
                    in reply, to express to you the satisfaction which is felt by the government at
                    the intelligence on this subject, which your communication conveys; not only in
                    the circumstance of the proposed abolition by Spain, but because this measure
                    must be looked upon as a great step to complete and universal emancipation.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
